## Compiled JavaScript files
#
# Scoped to real build output. This was `**/*.js`, which also hid hand-written
# source: jest.config.rules.js and jest.config.integration.js could not be
# committed without -f, so `npm run test:rules` / `test:integration` referenced
# configs that did not exist in a fresh clone and ~2.3k lines of security-rules
# tests never ran. jest.config.js and jest.setup.js are tracked only because
# they were force-added. The `!scripts/*.js` negation that used to live here was
# a patch for the same over-broad rule and is no longer needed.
#
# Artifact list matches the one in the root CLAUDE.md "Gotchas" section.
**/lib/**/*.js
**/dist/**/*.js
**/build/**/*.js
**/public/**/*.js
**/*.min.js
**/*-es5.js
**/*-es2015.js
**/*.js.map

# Typescript v1 declaration files
typings/

node_modules/
# Git worktrees
.worktrees/

# Firebase debug logs
firebase-debug.log
ui-debug.log

# Environment variables — never commit (may contain live keys)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
scripts/.env
